\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\par
\b Positional Encoding\par
\b0 Since Transformers process all words at once, they need a way to understand word order.\par
For example:\par
Dog bites man\par
and\par
Man bites dog\par
contain the same words but have different meanings.\par
\b Positional Encoding\b0  gives each word information about its position within the sequence.\par
\par
\b How GPT Uses Transformers\par
\b0 GPT stands for:\par
\b Generative Pre-trained Transformer\b0\par
GPT primarily uses the \b decoder portion\b0  of the Transformer architecture.\par
Workflow:\par
Input Prompt\par
\~\~\~\~\~ \f2\u8595?\f1\lang16393\par
Transformer Layers\par
\~\~\~\~\~ \f2\u8595?\f1\lang16393\par
Predict Next Token\par
\~\~\~\~\~ \f2\u8595?\f1\lang16393\par
Generate Response\par
Example:\par
The capital of France is\par
GPT predicts:\par
Paris\par
and continues generating text one token at a time.\par
